te-props\": [\"error\", \"consistent-as-needed\"],\r\n    \"no-undefined\": \"error\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What did you do? Please include the actual source code causing the issue.**\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste the source code below: -->\r\n```js\r\n'use strict';\r\n\r\nvar foo = {\r\n  undefined: 'bar',\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What did you expect to happen?**\r\n`undefined` should be permitted as an unquoted object property.\r\n\r\n**What actually happened? Please include the actual, raw output from ESLint.**\r\n`no-undefined` produces an error. Quoting `undefined` (which would otherwise be a workaround) produces an error from `quote-props`.\r\n\r\nGiven that `undefined` is a permissable object property name, I believe `no-undefined` should be modified to permit this behaviour.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"alberto","id":72561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto","html_url":"https://github.com/alberto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alberto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7964/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7964/timeline","performed_via_github_ap